{{/*
    providers.tmpl renders, for an Objective-C class that has subclasses, a sealed
    interface used to accept "any of its subclasses" as a method or property
    value. The interface requires the base's unexported marker method, which only
    the base class defines and its subclasses promote through embedding — so a
    setter typed as the provider accepts a real member of the hierarchy and
    nothing else.
*/}}
{{define "providers"}}{{range .Items}}// {{.IfaceName}} is accepted wherever a {{.BaseName}} (or one of its subclasses) is expected.
type {{.IfaceName}} interface {
objref.Object
{{.MarkerName}}()
}

{{end}}{{end}}
